ssional  success I often feel inadequate do you  might be sat there wondering well why  should I care and I'd say you should  care for two reasons as Future Business  Leaders you are going to miss out on  great talent and as humans you have a  responsibility to the young people in  your lives so because I'm an MBA student  I'm gonna start with a business case and  then talk about the human case so the  business case we are in an employee  market organizations are struggling to  fill their ranks in 2015 5 million US  jobs went unfilled but 8.5 million  Americans were looking for jobs  anybody else see them as much talented  people locked out of the workplace  workplaces struggling to find talented  people it is in no one's best interest  to only recruit from traditional paths  by broadening your criteria you're  opening yourself to capable and diverse  candidates 80% of job applications in  the United States ask for an associate's  degree or higher yet 42% of high school  sophomores graduate college do you see  the mismatch I get it it's hard to drive  change it is hard to open up systems  that include non-traditional backgrounds  it's hard but it's doable and you can't  afford not to by opening up your  recruitment criteria you are giving  yourself a competitive talent advantage  in this tight  employment market why not be the first  mover in this current talent war now  let's talk return on investment I urge  you to become the creators and not just  the consumers of tomorrow's talent by  that I mean we all have a responsibility  to not just use skills but build skills  there is more than just a business case  for employing people with an  untraditional background there's a  business case to build apprenticeship  programs in this business case is built  upon the value-added work that you will  get from teams that work on your  projects  it's from the value add that is given  from diversify teams we know that there  is return on investment that comes with  apprenticeship models it has been proven  and has been proven to come in as little  as 18 months so although that there is  costs associated with apprenticeship  programs things like wages training  costs and program management fees you  will see a positive return on investment  businesses need to push change from the  top down as humans we need to push  change from the bottom up college for  all is disadvantaging many young people  it is having a detrimental effect on  those that learn better by doing its  disadvantaging you at those that don't  have the means or the opportunity to  attend college apprenticeship programs  allow people to learn and giving  opportunities to people from all walks  of life apprenticeship programs can be  undertaken in health care construction  finance technology media even law there  is more than one way to success there  are multiple paths but they are  currently underfunded and under  recognized we are over indexing on one  so my us to you as Future Business  Leaders is why miss out on great talent  why not push for change and put your  money where your need is why not develop  programs to hire and train the  leaders of your organization and as  humans we need to challenge our elitist  attitudes that equate not having a  degree to not being capable we need to  recognize that apprenticeship programs  and work experience are just as valuable  as college degrees so I'm going to leave  you with three challenges I challenge  you to change the way you think about  non-traditional backgrounds I challenge  you to change the way you talk about  success and finally next time a resume  crosses your desk I challenge you not to  jump straight to education but instead  dig into experience and benefit from a  diverse young workforce thank you  [Applause]  [Music]

